cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Project Nūr in academic work, please cite it as below."
title: "Project Nūr: A Hybrid Cognitive Architecture for Relational Continuity in AI Assistants"
abstract: >-
  Project Nūr is an experimental cognitive architecture for AI assistants
  that treats emotion as persistent internal state rather than a stylistic
  prompt layer. It combines six continuous modulators (arousal, valence,
  certainty, bonding, energy, resolution), a dual memory system (short-term
  and long-term), unified self/other profiling, deterministic social
  appraisal, response strategy selection, bounded dual-process deliberation,
  and defense-mechanism-based expression shaping. The implementation is
  inspired by PSI Theory, ACT-R, and CLARION, but is presented as
  engineering-oriented synthesis rather than a faithful implementation of
  any one framework.
